<title>RUSSIA: Russia's LUKoil shoots up 12.2 pct to $21.00.</title>
<headline>Russia's LUKoil shoots up 12.2 pct to $21.00.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-06-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Russia's biggest oil company LUKoil, among the market's most liquid, jumped 12.2 percent at 0824 GMT on Wednesday to $21.00, from $18.71 at Tuesday's close.</p>
<p>Traders said LUKoil, which they said had trailed market growth in previous months, was benefiting from a wave of new foreign investment pouring into the Russian market over the past week.</p>
<p>--Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
</text>
